# Chongsu Valley terrain project

This addon contains the source package for a fictional North Korea-inspired
Enfusion terrain and planned valley city. The first-pass world is designed as
a 4,096 x 4,096 metre play space on a 2 metre terrain grid.

The generated package includes:

- a 2,049 x 2,049 ESRI ASCII height field with real metre elevations;
- a 16-bit PNG copy of the height field and an elevation manifest;
- satellite-style planning imagery and terrain surface masks;
- a measured, symmetrical city plan with vanilla building prefabs;
- Enfusion-ready road and building layer files;
- object-import data and GeoJSON reference data;
- a deterministic generator so the complete design can be rebuilt.

Run `Tools/generate_chongsu_valley.py` with a Python installation containing
NumPy and Pillow. See `Documentation/WORKBENCH_IMPORT.md` for the Enfusion
Workbench checkpoints that must be completed in the graphical editor.

The old `North Korea` addon elsewhere in the local addons directory was used
only as a read-only format reference. No files are copied from or written to
that project.
